/* book exam traps: Drawing the stall line as a straight line from the origin to VA. It is n = (V/VS1)², a parabola; a straight line under-predicts n at mid speeds. | Mirroring the top of the envelope to make the bottom. The negative stall line uses the smaller negative lift coefficient, and nmin rises from −1.0 at VC to 0 at VD for transport aircraft. | Ending the flat top at VC. For transport aircraft the positive limit nmax holds all the way to VD. | Ignoring gust lines at high speed. A gust point at VC can sit above the manoeuvre top, so the critical load may be a gust the pilot never commands. | Rounding VS1 too early. 57.14 × √2.5 = 90.35 m/s; using 57.1 gives 90.3 m/s. Keep full precision until the final answer. */
